            en: '{p1} may be describing the world while {p0} wants to start building, and an explanation that holds one child can lose the other. A long talk about how a plan might work can absorb one and feel like a delay to the other, and a task that fully absorbs one child can seem to the other to have ended the conversation.\n\nThe difference is in how each reaches the same place, not in how far each gets. {p0} can take the long description as a start that keeps being put off, and {p1} can take the quick first try as skipping the interesting part; each holds a half the other is missing.',
